1
00:00:00,928 --> 00:00:03,518
- Oh. Thank you, Penny.
- Mhmm.

2
00:00:03,697 --> 00:00:05,687
(Sheldon:)Yeah, wait. Here.

3
00:00:08,302 --> 00:00:09,792
(Sheldon:)For your troubles.

4
00:00:10,938 --> 00:00:13,138
(Penny:)Oh, boy, a whole dollar.

5
00:00:13,307 --> 00:00:14,827
(Penny:)Now I can quit my paper route.

6
00:00:16,644 --> 00:00:17,664
(Penny:)So, what's in it?

7
00:00:17,845 --> 00:00:21,835
(Leonard:)Doesn't matter. Half the time,
he just ends up playing with the box.

8
00:00:22,049 --> 00:00:25,419
(Sheldon:)Yeah, it's journals and research papers
I wrote as a child.

9
00:00:25,586 --> 00:00:27,456
(Penny:)Aw. How cute.

10
00:00:27,621 --> 00:00:29,141
(Penny:)Is this, like, a diary?

11
00:00:29,323 --> 00:00:31,913
No, that's my potty-training journal.

12
00:00:32,726 --> 00:00:35,316
- Really? Your potty-training journal?
- Yeah.

13
00:00:35,496 --> 00:00:39,456
(Sheldon:)And forgive my crude penmanship.
I didn't start typing until I was 6.

14
00:00:41,969 --> 00:00:43,899
"August 7th, 8:42 a.m.

15
00:00:44,071 --> 00:00:46,771
This is humiliating.
What was wrong with diapers?"

16
00:00:48,709 --> 00:00:50,539
(Sheldon:)There are some charts in the back...

17
00:00:50,711 --> 00:00:53,111
(Sheldon:)...where I kept track of shape,
color and consistency.

18
00:00:53,280 --> 00:00:54,610
(Leonard:)Oh!

19
00:00:55,716 --> 00:00:57,376
(Penny:)Disgusting.

20
00:00:57,551 --> 00:01:02,021
(Leonard:)No, what's disgusting
is he's still keeping track.

